  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 154 AM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nThe broad upper-level ridge will continue to retrograde/build \nwestward over much of the southern CONUS this weekend and will \nremain dominant through the middle of next week. Isolated to \nscattered afternoon and evening showers and thunderstorms may \ndevelop over the higher terrain areas of the western CWA this \nweekend, but overall coverage looks to become very few and far \nbetween over the higher terrain Monday through Wednesday. Hot and \ndry conditions will be prevalent over most of the forecast area \nthrough the extended period under the ridge. Highs continue to range \nin the upper 90s to around 102 degrees for most each day, with \nreadings in the lower 90s over mountain areas and 102-108 degrees \nalong the Rio Grande. Early morning lows will range in the 60s in \nthe mountains and in the 70s over the rest of the area.",
